/-!
# Normality of the coordinate ring of a nonsingular Weierstrass curve

`CoordinateRingDedekind.lean` proves `IsDedekindDomain W.CoordinateRing` modulo
`[IsIntegrallyClosed W.CoordinateRing]`. This file discharges that hypothesis as
far as mathlib currently allows: it reduces normality of `F[W]` to the
regularity of the local ring at each closed point, and composes the reduction
out of the mathlib lemmas that exist. The one input mathlib does not provide —
the Jacobian criterion tying nonsingularity of `W` to that local regularity —
is isolated as a single named predicate.

## The route

`IsIntegrallyClosed` is a local property: an integral domain is integrally
closed once every localization at a nonzero maximal ideal is
(`IsIntegrallyClosed.of_localization_maximal`). For the coordinate ring `F[W]`,
each such localization `(F[W])_p` is a Noetherian local domain that is integral
over the PID `F[X]`, hence one-dimensional. For a Noetherian local domain the
DVR characterization applies: `(F[W])_p` is a discrete valuation ring exactly
when its cotangent space `𝔪ₚ/𝔪ₚ²` is one-dimensional over the residue field
(`IsLocalRing.finrank_CotangentSpace_eq_one_iff`). A discrete valuation ring is
a principal ideal ring, hence a unique factorization monoid, hence integrally
closed. Composing these gives normality from the per-point cotangent condition.

The per-point cotangent condition is packaged as `RegularAtClosedPoints W`.

## Missing mathlib input

The predicate `RegularAtClosedPoints W` is the algebraic form of the Jacobian
nonsingularity criterion: for a nonsingular affine plane curve the local ring at
each point is regular of dimension one, i.e. its maximal ideal is generated by a
single element. Mathlib has neither the general hypersurface Jacobian criterion
nor any statement connecting the Weierstrass discriminant `W.Δ` (or the pointwise
`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Nonsingular`) to the cotangent space of a localization
of `W.CoordinateRing`. `IsRegularLocalRing` is defined
(`Mathlib/RingTheory/RegularLocalRing/Defs.lean`) but is used nowhere else, and
there is no "regular local ring ⇒ integrally closed" (Serre) transfer in mathlib.
The exact missing lemma is:

`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.CoordinateRing.regularAtClosedPoints_of_Δ_ne_zero` :
for `W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine F` with `W.Δ ≠ 0`, `RegularAtClosedPoints W`.

Its proof is the Jacobian criterion for the single defining relation
`W.polynomial`, evaluated at the residue field of each closed point: nonvanishing
of one of the partial derivatives `W.polynomialX`, `W.polynomialY` (which is
`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Nonsingular`, guaranteed at every solution by `W.Δ ≠ 0`
via `WeierstrassCurve.Affine.equation_iff_nonsingular_of_Δ_ne_zero`) forces the
maximal ideal of `(F[W])_p` to be principal.
-/

namespace WeierstrassCurve.Affine.CoordinateRing

open Polynomial Module IsLocalRing

variable {F : Type*} [Field F] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine F)

/-- Regularity of the coordinate ring `F[W]` at every closed point, phrased
through the cotangent space: for each nonzero maximal ideal `p` of `F[W]`, the
local ring `(F[W])_p` has a one-dimensional cotangent space `𝔪ₚ/𝔪ₚ²` over its
residue field. This is the algebraic content of the Jacobian nonsingularity
criterion for the affine plane curve `W`. -/
def RegularAtClosedPoints : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : Ideal W.CoordinateRing) (_ : p ≠ ⊥) [p.IsMaximal],
    finrank (ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p))
      (CotangentSpace (Localization.AtPrime p)) = 1

/-- The localization of the coordinate ring at a nonzero maximal ideal whose
cotangent space is one-dimensional is a discrete valuation ring. -/
theorem isDiscreteValuationRing_localization_of_finrank_cotangentSpace_eq_one
    {p : Ideal W.CoordinateRing} [p.IsMaximal]
    (hp : finrank (ResidueField (Localization.AtPrime p))
      (CotangentSpace (Localization.AtPrime p)) = 1) :
    IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime p) := by
  haveI : IsNoetherianRing (Localization.AtPrime p) :=
    IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing p.primeCompl _ inferInstance
  exact IsLocalRing.finrank_CotangentSpace_eq_one_iff.mp hp

/-- If the coordinate ring `F[W]` is regular at every closed point, then it is
integrally closed. The localization at each nonzero maximal ideal is a discrete
valuation ring, hence a principal ideal ring, hence integrally closed; and
integral closedness is a local property
(`IsIntegrallyClosed.of_localization_maximal`). -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_of_regularAtClosedPoints
    (hReg : RegularAtClosedPoints W) : IsIntegrallyClosed W.CoordinateRing := by
  apply IsIntegrallyClosed.of_localization_maximal
  intro p hp _
  haveI : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime p) :=
    isDiscreteValuationRing_localization_of_finrank_cotangentSpace_eq_one W (hReg p hp)
  infer_instance

end WeierstrassCurve.Affine.CoordinateRing
